WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.833
(uplifting music)

00:00:04.259 --> 00:00:05.629
- When I tell people that I'm a wrestler

00:00:05.629 --> 00:00:07.189
they don't really believe me at first.

00:00:07.189 --> 00:00:09.229
I don't know what image
they have in their head

00:00:09.229 --> 00:00:11.691
of what a wrestler should look like.

00:00:11.691 --> 00:00:13.539
Especially when I say
I'm the super heavyweight

00:00:13.539 --> 00:00:14.550
for women's wrestling.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:15.969
And they're like, "You wrestle,

00:00:15.969 --> 00:00:18.069
you're kind of too pretty to wrestle".

00:00:18.069 --> 00:00:19.699
It's always interesting
to me, 'cause I'm like,

00:00:19.699 --> 00:00:21.532
"What did you expect?"

00:00:27.619 --> 00:00:30.202
(upbeat music)

00:00:31.369 --> 00:00:34.118
My name's Adeline Gray, I'm
a three-time world champion.

00:00:34.118 --> 00:00:35.545
Ranked number one in the world,

00:00:35.545 --> 00:00:36.989
been undefeated for two and a half years.

00:00:36.989 --> 00:00:40.457
And I'm gonna compete in the
Rio Olympic Games in August.

00:00:40.457 --> 00:00:42.760
I never really considered the
Olympics as an option for me

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.859
when I was a younger kid and
it's something that I don't

00:00:44.859 --> 00:00:47.667
think enough girls have an
opportunity to dream about.

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:50.250
(upbeat music)

00:00:52.848 --> 00:00:55.059
I want to redefine feminine to some extent

00:00:55.059 --> 00:00:57.240
and to have people challenge the way

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.931
they look at the word strong

00:00:58.931 --> 00:01:02.931
and not just see a boy
that pops into your head.

00:01:07.211 --> 00:01:08.931
I started wrestling boys
when I was six years old

00:01:08.931 --> 00:01:12.163
and I wrestled boys all the
way through high school.

00:01:12.163 --> 00:01:14.746
(upbeat music)

00:01:16.529 --> 00:01:18.371
And I think I earned a lot
of respect from a lot of

00:01:18.371 --> 00:01:21.870
the teammates out there who
did lose to me or maybe beat me

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:25.200
and I got to train with
the best guys in the world

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.701
and they made me tougher.

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:28.480
They made me work for every single point

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.400
I had to wrestle with and
they made it so that I could

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.650
be a champion on the women's level now.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.808
We teach girls to be perfect
and boys to take risks.

00:01:38.808 --> 00:01:41.600
I need to take risks, that
I am a confident and strong

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.832
female who knows that
I'm great at wrestling.

00:01:43.832 --> 00:01:45.729
And I'm still struggling
with that concept that

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:49.896
I'm worried about not being
perfect when I step on the mat.

00:01:52.072 --> 00:01:54.989
(soft piano music)

00:01:58.589 --> 00:02:01.379
I have to step on that mat
and make sure that I work

00:02:01.379 --> 00:02:05.462
every single moment to
win an Olympic gold medal.

00:02:07.906 --> 00:02:11.091
I want young girls to be
able to look at that, my situation

00:02:11.091 --> 00:02:13.587
and be able to dream about it.

00:02:13.587 --> 00:02:16.301
I'm excited for that moment
to have my flag risen

00:02:16.301 --> 00:02:18.280
and be able to know that I'm gonna

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.800
hold a gold medal around my neck.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.717
(soft piano music)

